<title>USA: Albany Cty, N.Y. plans $52 mln renovation - paper.</title>
<headline>Albany Cty, N.Y. plans $52 mln renovation - paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Albany County, N.Y., plans to spend as much as $52 million by 2001 to renovate buildings, roads and towns, Albany Times Union reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said the five-year capital plan sets aside $38 million for courthouses, and $9 million for the phase three expansion and renovation of the Albany County Correctional Facility.</p>
<p>Legislators were given the authority to issue bonds for any projects that total more than $250,000, but county executives do not have to spend all of the money, it said.</p>
<p>It quoted Robert Lawton, policy analyst for Albany County Executive Michael Breslin as saying that the plan represented the &quot;outer limits&quot; of county spending.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
